Z||000000||biggdaddy||08-14-99||11:24 AM||||<br>could anyone of you mechanical tech pros give me the lowdown on which mods are worth it and approx how much $$$ I will have to dish out.  I have a black 85 gt 4 spd.    THANKS!!
Z||000001||batboy||08-14-99||11:50 AM||||I'd start with the basics, thoroughly check everything, especially mechanical parts, brakes, steering, and suspension. Replace anything that looks like it has wear on it. A better flowing and sounding exhaust system is another good place to start, unless you plan on dropping the engine out soon. That ought to keep you busy for a while.<p>There are several different approaches to upgrading the Fiero. High performance mods, handling mods, brake mods, exterior body mods, and stereo systems. Of course these can be mixed and matched. What kind of car do you want?
Z||000002||biggdaddy||08-15-99||02:16 PM||||engine`s already dropped now... was thinking headers and porting for starters? worth it? any alternatives? <br>I`m looking to build a mean lookin` great handling machine with enough power to not make a fool of myself should the need for a little red light competitiveness arise. (already made up my mind about exterior mods: rear decklid scoop, supra style wing to replace gt wing, side scoops, chin spoiler and perhaps a non-popup headlight front hood with scoops of course.  Maybe even wider front and rear fenders to accomodate bigger wheels. But that`s starting to get expensive.) Found all these body mods on the net, prices not to bad any idea where the best prices are?<br>                  thanks batboy<br>p.s. A guy up here (montreal) has a full blown replica batmobile, and I think he said that it can be done on a fiero.  I`ll try and find out next time I speak to him.
