Z||000036||lowCG||08-21-99||12:43 AM||||There's always going to be someone faster than you,but if your suspension were to be maximised,you'd at least be truly happy with the way your car goes down the road.It's only a matter of correct spring rates,shocks,and tires in a Fiero to achieve the equivalent enjoyment of a Pro-Stock motor on the street.<br>A lot more reliable too.<br>If you want to go fast,get a Suzuki GS motorcycle,or a big block corvette,the 2.8 is decent as a stock motor,but I just can't seem to appreciate the idea of scraped knuckles,or loss of sleep over trying to get a couple of extra horsepower out of that motor.<br>Well maybe a cam,and a little bit of headwork,but nothing else!
Z||000037||Pretender||08-22-99||03:54 AM||||ahh rice burners., my other passion, i'm only driving my fiero because an 86 yrl. woman seemed to total my '89 Conguest, and NO FIERO would ever dream about beating me unless it's a blown big block on N20 but the suspension is what gets my atttention, I own an 88 gt and it hugs the road perfect, i've owned a lot of rear wheel drive sports (never driven front wheel drive)*honest* cars and although the fiero lacks in power it is the best handling car i've ever driven, My best friend just bought a ' 91 mr2*new bodie* and it seems to handle a smidge better in the turns but i think it has power steering in which i would rather give up, i love my steering and the traction control of the rear., does anyone have the stats of this car?. it will be the next car i'll own but i will never get rid  of my 88gt., NEVER!. It wi;; be a 12 sec. sleeper "street car" someday soon. And i use a K&N!.*S*
